{"stanza_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Alas! and did my Saviour bleed, and did my Sovereign die?", "char_len": 57, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/alas_and_did_my_savior_bleed", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Was it for crimes that I had done He groaned upon the tree?", "char_len": 59, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/alas_and_did_my_savior_bleed", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Well might the sun in darkness hide, and shut his glories in,", "char_len": 61, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/alas_and_did_my_savior_bleed", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-alas-and-did-my-saviour-bleed", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "But drops of grief can ne'er repay the debt of love I owe:", "char_len": 58, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/alas_and_did_my_savior_bleed", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "When I survey the wondrous cross on which the Prince of glory died,", "char_len": 67, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_i_survey_the_wondrous_cross_watts", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Forbid it, Lord, that I should boast, save in the death of Christ my God;", "char_len": 73, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_i_survey_the_wondrous_cross_watts", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "See, from His head, His hands, His feet, sorrow and love flow mingled down;", "char_len": 75, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_i_survey_the_wondrous_cross_watts", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-survey-the-wondrous-cross", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "Were the whole realm of nature mine, that were a present far too small;", "char_len": 71, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_i_survey_the_wondrous_cross_watts", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "There is a fountain filled with blood drawn from Immanuel's veins;", "char_len": 66, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/there_is_a_fountain_filled_with_blood", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "The dying thief rejoiced to see that fountain in his day;", "char_len": 57, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/there_is_a_fountain_filled_with_blood", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Dear dying Lamb, Thy precious blood shall never lose its power,", "char_len": 63, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/there_is_a_fountain_filled_with_blood", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-there-is-a-fountain-filled-with-blood", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "E'er since by faith I saw the stream Thy flowing wounds supply,", "char_len": 63, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/there_is_a_fountain_filled_with_blood", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "How sweet the Name of Jesus sounds in a believer's ear!", "char_len": 55, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_sweet_the_name_of_jesus_sounds", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "It makes the wounded spirit whole, and calms the troubled breast;", "char_len": 65, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_sweet_the_name_of_jesus_sounds", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Dear Name! the rock on which I build, my shield and hiding place,", "char_len": 65, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_sweet_the_name_of_jesus_sounds", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-how-sweet-the-name-of-jesus-sounds", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "Jesus, my Shepherd, Husband, Friend, my Prophet, Priest, and King,", "char_len": 66, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_sweet_the_name_of_jesus_sounds", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-amazing-grace-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-amazing-grace", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Amazing grace! how sweet the sound that saved a wretch like me!", "char_len": 63, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/amazing_grace_how_sweet_the_sound", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-amazing-grace-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-amazing-grace", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Twas grace that taught my heart to fear, and grace my fears relieved;", "char_len": 69, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/amazing_grace_how_sweet_the_sound", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-amazing-grace-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-amazing-grace", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Through many dangers, toils, and snares, I have already come;", "char_len": 61, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/amazing_grace_how_sweet_the_sound", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-amazing-grace-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-amazing-grace", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "The Lord has promised good to me, His word my hope secures;", "char_len": 59, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/amazing_grace_how_sweet_the_sound", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "All hail the power of Jesus' name! Let angels prostrate fall;", "char_len": 61, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/all_hail_the_power_of_jesus_name", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Ye chosen seed of Israel's race, ye ransomed from the fall,", "char_len": 59, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/all_hail_the_power_of_jesus_name", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Let every kindred, every tribe, on this terrestrial ball,", "char_len": 57, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/all_hail_the_power_of_jesus_name", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-all-hail-the-power-of-jesus-name", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "O that with yonder sacred throng we at His feet may fall!", "char_len": 57, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/all_hail_the_power_of_jesus_name", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Holy, holy, holy! Lord God Almighty! Early in the morning our song shall rise to Thee;", "char_len": 86, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/holy_holy_holy_lord_god_almighty", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Holy, holy, holy! all the saints adore Thee, casting down their golden crowns around the glassy sea;", "char_len": 100, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/holy_holy_holy_lord_god_almighty", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Holy, holy, holy! though the darkness hide Thee, though the eye of sinful man Thy glory may not see;", "char_len": 100, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/holy_holy_holy_lord_god_almighty", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-holy-holy-holy", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "Holy, holy, holy! Lord God Almighty! All Thy works shall praise Thy name in earth and sky and sea;", "char_len": 98, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/holy_holy_holy_lord_god_almighty", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-abide-with-me-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-abide-with-me", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Abide with me: fast falls the eventide; the darkness deepens; Lord, with me abide.", "char_len": 82, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/abide_with_me_fast_falls_the_eventide", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-abide-with-me-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-abide-with-me", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Swift to its close ebbs out life's little day; earth's joys grow dim, its glories pass away;", "char_len": 92, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/abide_with_me_fast_falls_the_eventide", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-abide-with-me-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-abide-with-me", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "I need Thy presence every passing hour; what but Thy grace can foil the tempter's power?", "char_len": 88, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/abide_with_me_fast_falls_the_eventide", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-abide-with-me-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-abide-with-me", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "Hold Thou Thy cross before my closing eyes; shine through the gloom, and point me to the skies;", "char_len": 95, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/abide_with_me_fast_falls_the_eventide", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-rock-of-ages-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-rock-of-ages", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Rock of Ages, cleft for me, let me hide myself in Thee;", "char_len": 55, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/rock_of_ages_cleft_for_me_let", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-rock-of-ages-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-rock-of-ages", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Not the labors of my hands can fulfill Thy law's demands;", "char_len": 57, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/rock_of_ages_cleft_for_me_let", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-rock-of-ages-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-rock-of-ages", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Nothing in my hand I bring, simply to Thy cross I cling;", "char_len": 56, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/rock_of_ages_cleft_for_me_let", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-rock-of-ages-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-rock-of-ages", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "While I draw this fleeting breath, when my eyes shall close in death,", "char_len": 69, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/rock_of_ages_cleft_for_me_let", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-just-as-i-am-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-just-as-i-am", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Just as I am, without one plea, but that Thy blood was shed for me,", "char_len": 67, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/just_as_i_am_without_one_plea", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-just-as-i-am-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-just-as-i-am", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Just as I am, and waiting not to rid my soul of one dark blot,", "char_len": 62, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/just_as_i_am_without_one_plea", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-just-as-i-am-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-just-as-i-am", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Just as I am, though tossed about with many a conflict, many a doubt,", "char_len": 69, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/just_as_i_am_without_one_plea", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-just-as-i-am-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-just-as-i-am", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "Just as I am, Thou wilt receive, wilt welcome, pardon, cleanse, relieve;", "char_len": 72, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/just_as_i_am_without_one_plea", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Christ our Redeemer died on the cross, died for the sinner, paid all his due;", "char_len": 77, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/christ_our_redeemer_died_on_the_cross", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Chiefest of sinners, Jesus will save; all He has promised, that He will do;", "char_len": 75, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/christ_our_redeemer_died_on_the_cross", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Judgment is coming, all will be there, who have rejected, who have refused;", "char_len": 75, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/christ_our_redeemer_died_on_the_cross", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-see-the-blood", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "O what a Saviour, that He died for me! From condemnation He hath made me free;", "char_len": 78, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/christ_our_redeemer_died_on_the_cross", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-a-debtor-to-mercy-alone-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-a-debtor-to-mercy-alone", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "A debtor to mercy alone, of covenant mercy I sing;", "char_len": 50, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_debtor_to_mercy_alone", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-a-debtor-to-mercy-alone-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-a-debtor-to-mercy-alone", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "The work which His goodness began, the arm of His strength will complete;", "char_len": 73, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_debtor_to_mercy_alone", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-a-debtor-to-mercy-alone-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-a-debtor-to-mercy-alone", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "My name from the palms of His hands eternity will not erase;", "char_len": 60, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_debtor_to_mercy_alone", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-a-mind-at-perfect-peace-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-a-mind-at-perfect-peace", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "A mind at perfect peace with God: O what a word is this!", "char_len": 56, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_mind_at_perfect_peace_with_god", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-a-mind-at-perfect-peace-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-a-mind-at-perfect-peace", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "By nature and by practice far, how very far from God!", "char_len": 53, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_mind_at_perfect_peace_with_god", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-a-mind-at-perfect-peace-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-a-mind-at-perfect-peace", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "So near, so very near to God, I cannot nearer be;", "char_len": 49, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/a_mind_at_perfect_peace_with_god", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "According to Thy gracious word, in meek humility,", "char_len": 49, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/according_to_thy_gracious_word", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Thy body broken for my sake, my bread from heaven shall be;", "char_len": 59, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/according_to_thy_gracious_word", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Gethsemane can I forget? Or there Thy conflict see,", "char_len": 51, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/according_to_thy_gracious_word", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-according-to-thy-gracious-word", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "When to the cross I turn my eyes, and rest on Calvary,", "char_len": 54, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/according_to_thy_gracious_word", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "bhb-classic-023-s01", "hymn_id": "bhb-classic-023", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Beneath the cross of Jesus I fain would take my stand,", "char_len": 54, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/beneath_the_cross_of_jesus", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "bhb-classic-023-s02", "hymn_id": "bhb-classic-023", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "O safe and happy shelter! O refuge tried and sweet!", "char_len": 51, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/beneath_the_cross_of_jesus", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "bhb-classic-023-s03", "hymn_id": "bhb-classic-023", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Upon that cross of Jesus mine eye at times can see", "char_len": 50, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/beneath_the_cross_of_jesus", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "bhb-classic-023-s04", "hymn_id": "bhb-classic-023", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "I take, O cross, thy shadow for my abiding place;", "char_len": 49, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/beneath_the_cross_of_jesus", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "How firm a foundation, ye saints of the Lord, is laid for your faith in His excellent word!", "char_len": 91, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_firm_a_foundation_ye_saints_of", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Fear not, I am with thee, O be not dismayed, for I am thy God, and will still give thee aid;", "char_len": 92, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_firm_a_foundation_ye_saints_of", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "When through the deep waters I call thee to go, the rivers of sorrow shall not overflow;", "char_len": 88, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_firm_a_foundation_ye_saints_of", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-how-firm-a-foundation", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "The soul that on Jesus hath leaned for repose I will not, I will not desert to his foes;", "char_len": 88, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/how_firm_a_foundation_ye_saints_of", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-o-god-our-help-in-ages-past-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-o-god-our-help-in-ages-past", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "O God, our help in ages past, our hope for years to come,", "char_len": 57, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/o_god_our_help_in_ages_past", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-o-god-our-help-in-ages-past-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-o-god-our-help-in-ages-past", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Under the shadow of Thy throne Thy saints have dwelt secure;", "char_len": 60, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/o_god_our_help_in_ages_past", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-o-god-our-help-in-ages-past-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-o-god-our-help-in-ages-past", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Before the hills in order stood, or earth received her frame,", "char_len": 61, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/o_god_our_help_in_ages_past", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-o-god-our-help-in-ages-past-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-o-god-our-help-in-ages-past", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "A thousand ages in Thy sight are like an evening gone;", "char_len": 54, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/o_god_our_help_in_ages_past", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-guide-me-o-thou-great-jehovah-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-guide-me-o-thou-great-jehovah", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Guide me, O Thou great Jehovah, pilgrim through this barren land;", "char_len": 65, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/guide_me_o_thou_great_jehovah", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-guide-me-o-thou-great-jehovah-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-guide-me-o-thou-great-jehovah", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Open now the crystal fountain, whence the healing stream doth flow;", "char_len": 67, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/guide_me_o_thou_great_jehovah", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-guide-me-o-thou-great-jehovah-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-guide-me-o-thou-great-jehovah", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "When I tread the verge of Jordan, bid my anxious fears subside;", "char_len": 63, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/guide_me_o_thou_great_jehovah", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-man-of-sorrows-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-man-of-sorrows", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Man of Sorrows! what a name for the Son of God, who came", "char_len": 56, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/man_of_sorrows_what_a_name", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-man-of-sorrows-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-man-of-sorrows", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Bearing shame and scoffing rude, in my place condemned He stood;", "char_len": 64, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/man_of_sorrows_what_a_name", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-man-of-sorrows-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-man-of-sorrows", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Guilty, vile, and helpless we; spotless Lamb of God was He;", "char_len": 59, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/man_of_sorrows_what_a_name", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-man-of-sorrows-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-man-of-sorrows", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "Lifted up was He to die, It is finished was His cry;", "char_len": 52, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/man_of_sorrows_what_a_name", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-it-is-well-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-it-is-well", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "When peace like a river attendeth my way, when sorrows like sea billows roll,", "char_len": 77, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_peace_like_a_river_attendeth_my", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-it-is-well-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-it-is-well", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Though Satan should buffet, though trials should come, let this blest assurance control,", "char_len": 88, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_peace_like_a_river_attendeth_my", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-it-is-well-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-it-is-well", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "My sin—O the bliss of this glorious thought!—my sin, not in part, but the whole,", "char_len": 80, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_peace_like_a_river_attendeth_my", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-it-is-well-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-it-is-well", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "And Lord, haste the day when the faith shall be sight, the clouds be rolled back as a scroll,", "char_len": 93, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/when_peace_like_a_river_attendeth_my", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-what-a-friend-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-what-a-friend", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "What a friend we have in Jesus, all our sins and griefs to bear!", "char_len": 64, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/what_a_friend_we_have_in_jesus_all_o", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-what-a-friend-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-what-a-friend", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Have we trials and temptations? Is there trouble anywhere?", "char_len": 58, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/what_a_friend_we_have_in_jesus_all_o", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-what-a-friend-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-what-a-friend", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Are we weak and heavy-laden, cumbered with a load of care?", "char_len": 58, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/what_a_friend_we_have_in_jesus_all_o", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-i-heard-the-voice-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-i-heard-the-voice", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "I heard the voice of Jesus say, Come unto Me and rest;", "char_len": 54, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/i_heard_the_voice_of_jesus_say_come", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-i-heard-the-voice-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-i-heard-the-voice", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "I heard the voice of Jesus say, Behold, I freely give", "char_len": 53, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/i_heard_the_voice_of_jesus_say_come", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-i-heard-the-voice-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-i-heard-the-voice", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "I heard the voice of Jesus say, I am this dark world's Light;", "char_len": 61, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/i_heard_the_voice_of_jesus_say_come", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-what-can-wash-away-my-sin-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-what-can-wash-away-my-sin", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "What can wash away my sin? Nothing but the blood of Jesus;", "char_len": 58, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/what_can_wash_away_my_sin", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-what-can-wash-away-my-sin-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-what-can-wash-away-my-sin", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "For my pardon this I see: nothing but the blood of Jesus;", "char_len": 57, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/what_can_wash_away_my_sin", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-what-can-wash-away-my-sin-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-what-can-wash-away-my-sin", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Nothing can for sin atone: nothing but the blood of Jesus;", "char_len": 58, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/what_can_wash_away_my_sin", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-what-can-wash-away-my-sin-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-what-can-wash-away-my-sin", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "This is all my hope and peace: nothing but the blood of Jesus;", "char_len": 62, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/what_can_wash_away_my_sin", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-i-stand-amazed-in-the-presence-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-i-stand-amazed-in-the-presence", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "I stand amazed in the presence of Jesus the Nazarene,", "char_len": 53, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/i_stand_amazed_in_the_presence", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-i-stand-amazed-in-the-presence-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-i-stand-amazed-in-the-presence", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "For me it was in the garden He prayed, Not My will, but Thine;", "char_len": 62, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/i_stand_amazed_in_the_presence", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-i-stand-amazed-in-the-presence-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-i-stand-amazed-in-the-presence", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "He took my sins and my sorrows, He made them His very own;", "char_len": 58, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/i_stand_amazed_in_the_presence", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-yet-there-is-room-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-yet-there-is-room", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Yet there is room! The Lamb's bright hall of song, with its fair glory, beckons thee along;", "char_len": 91, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/yet_there_is_room_the_lambs_bright", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-yet-there-is-room-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-yet-there-is-room", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Day is declining, and the Saviour cries: Room for the weary, room for thee;", "char_len": 75, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/yet_there_is_room_the_lambs_bright", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-yet-there-is-room-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-yet-there-is-room", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Room, room, still room! O enter, enter now; room, room, still room!", "char_len": 67, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/yet_there_is_room_the_lambs_bright", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-weve-a-story-to-tell-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-weve-a-story-to-tell", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "We've a story to tell to the nations that shall turn their hearts to the right,", "char_len": 79, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/weve_a_story_to_tell_to_the_nations", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-weve-a-story-to-tell-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-weve-a-story-to-tell", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "We've a song to be sung to the nations that shall lift their hearts to the Lord,", "char_len": 80, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/weve_a_story_to_tell_to_the_nations", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-weve-a-story-to-tell-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-weve-a-story-to-tell", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "We've a message to give to the nations, that the Lord who reigneth above", "char_len": 72, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/weve_a_story_to_tell_to_the_nations", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-my-faith-has-found-a-resting-place-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-my-faith-has-found-a-resting-place", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "My faith has found a resting place, not in device or creed;", "char_len": 59, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/my_faith_has_found_a_resting_place", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-my-faith-has-found-a-resting-place-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-my-faith-has-found-a-resting-place", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Enough for me that Jesus saves, this ends my fear and doubt;", "char_len": 60, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/my_faith_has_found_a_resting_place", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-my-faith-has-found-a-resting-place-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-my-faith-has-found-a-resting-place", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "My heart is leaning on the Word, the written Word of God,", "char_len": 57, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/my_faith_has_found_a_resting_place", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-one-there-is-above-all-others-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-one-there-is-above-all-others", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "One there is above all others, well deserves the name of Friend;", "char_len": 64, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/one_there_is_above_all_others_o_how_he", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-one-there-is-above-all-others-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-one-there-is-above-all-others", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Which of all our friends, to save us, could or would have shed his blood?", "char_len": 73, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/one_there_is_above_all_others_o_how_he", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-one-there-is-above-all-others-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-one-there-is-above-all-others", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "When He lived on earth abased, Friend of sinners was His name;", "char_len": 62, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/one_there_is_above_all_others_o_how_he", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-jesus-lover-of-my-soul-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-jesus-lover-of-my-soul", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Jesus, Lover of my soul, let me to Thy bosom fly,", "char_len": 49, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/jesus_lover_of_my_soul_let_me_to", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-jesus-lover-of-my-soul-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-jesus-lover-of-my-soul", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Other refuge have I none; hangs my helpless soul on Thee;", "char_len": 57, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/jesus_lover_of_my_soul_let_me_to", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-jesus-lover-of-my-soul-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-jesus-lover-of-my-soul", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Thou, O Christ, art all I want; more than all in Thee I find;", "char_len": 61, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/jesus_lover_of_my_soul_let_me_to", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-blessed-assurance-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-blessed-assurance", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Blessed assurance, Jesus is mine! O what a foretaste of glory divine!", "char_len": 69, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/blessed_assurance_jesus_is_mine", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-blessed-assurance-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-blessed-assurance", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Perfect submission, perfect delight, visions of rapture now burst on my sight;", "char_len": 78, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/blessed_assurance_jesus_is_mine", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-blessed-assurance-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-blessed-assurance", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Perfect submission, all is at rest, I in my Saviour am happy and blest;", "char_len": 71, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/blessed_assurance_jesus_is_mine", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-nearer-my-god-to-thee-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-nearer-my-god-to-thee", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Nearer, my God, to Thee, nearer to Thee! E'en though it be a cross that raiseth me,", "char_len": 83, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/nearer_my_god_to_thee_nearer_to", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-nearer-my-god-to-thee-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-nearer-my-god-to-thee", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Though like the wanderer, the sun gone down, darkness be over me, my rest a stone,", "char_len": 82, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/nearer_my_god_to_thee_nearer_to", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-nearer-my-god-to-thee-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-nearer-my-god-to-thee", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "There let the way appear steps unto heaven; all that Thou sendest me in mercy given;", "char_len": 84, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/nearer_my_god_to_thee_nearer_to", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-crown-him-with-many-crowns-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-crown-him-with-many-crowns", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Crown Him with many crowns, the Lamb upon His throne;", "char_len": 53, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/crown_him_with_many_crowns", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-crown-him-with-many-crowns-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-crown-him-with-many-crowns", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Crown Him the Lord of love; behold His hands and side,", "char_len": 54, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/crown_him_with_many_crowns", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-crown-him-with-many-crowns-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-crown-him-with-many-crowns", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Crown Him the Lord of life, who triumphed o'er the grave,", "char_len": 57, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/crown_him_with_many_crowns", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-come-thou-fount-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-come-thou-fount", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Come, Thou Fount of every blessing, tune my heart to sing Thy grace;", "char_len": 68, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/come_thou_fount_of_every_blessing", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-come-thou-fount-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-come-thou-fount", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Here I raise my Ebenezer; hither by Thy help I'm come;", "char_len": 54, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/come_thou_fount_of_every_blessing", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-come-thou-fount-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-come-thou-fount", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "O to grace how great a debtor daily I'm constrained to be!", "char_len": 58, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/come_thou_fount_of_every_blessing", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-the-lords-my-shepherd-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-the-lords-my-shepherd", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "The Lord's my Shepherd, I'll not want; He makes me down to lie", "char_len": 62, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/the_lords_my_shepherd_ill_not_want", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-the-lords-my-shepherd-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-the-lords-my-shepherd", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "My soul He doth restore again, and me to walk doth make", "char_len": 55, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/the_lords_my_shepherd_ill_not_want", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-the-lords-my-shepherd-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-the-lords-my-shepherd", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Yea, though I walk in death's dark vale, yet will I fear none ill;", "char_len": 66, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/the_lords_my_shepherd_ill_not_want", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-be-thou-my-vision-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-be-thou-my-vision", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Be Thou my Vision, O Lord of my heart; naught be all else to me, save that Thou art;", "char_len": 84, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/be_thou_my_vision_o_lord_of_my_heart", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-be-thou-my-vision-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-be-thou-my-vision", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Be Thou my Wisdom, and Thou my true Word; I ever with Thee and Thou with me, Lord;", "char_len": 82, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/be_thou_my_vision_o_lord_of_my_heart", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-be-thou-my-vision-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-be-thou-my-vision", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Riches I heed not, nor man's empty praise; Thou mine inheritance, now and always;", "char_len": 81, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/be_thou_my_vision_o_lord_of_my_heart", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-fairest-lord-jesus-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-fairest-lord-jesus", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Fairest Lord Jesus, Ruler of all nature, O Thou of God and man the Son,", "char_len": 71, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/fairest_lord_jesus_ruler_of_all_nature", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-fairest-lord-jesus-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-fairest-lord-jesus", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Fair are the meadows, fairer still the woodlands, robed in the blooming garb of spring;", "char_len": 87, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/fairest_lord_jesus_ruler_of_all_nature", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-fairest-lord-jesus-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-fairest-lord-jesus", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Fair is the sunshine, fairer still the moonlight, and all the twinkling starry host;", "char_len": 84, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/fairest_lord_jesus_ruler_of_all_nature", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-jesus-shall-reign-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-jesus-shall-reign", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Jesus shall reign where'er the sun does his successive journeys run;", "char_len": 68, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/jesus_shall_reign_whereer_the_sun", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-jesus-shall-reign-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-jesus-shall-reign", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "To Him shall endless prayer be made, and praises throng to crown His head;", "char_len": 74, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/jesus_shall_reign_whereer_the_sun", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-jesus-shall-reign-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-jesus-shall-reign", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "People and realms of every tongue dwell on His love with sweetest song;", "char_len": 71, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/jesus_shall_reign_whereer_the_sun", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-when-i-survey-brethren-table-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-survey-brethren-table", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Around Thy table, holy Lord, in sweet communion draw near,", "char_len": 58, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/around_thy_table_holy_lord", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-when-i-survey-brethren-table-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-survey-brethren-table", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Here every one that loves Thy name our willing thanks may bring;", "char_len": 64, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/around_thy_table_holy_lord", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-when-i-survey-brethren-table-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-when-i-survey-brethren-table", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "O Lord, what love is this of Thine, that draws us to Thy feet!", "char_len": 62, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/around_thy_table_holy_lord", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-glory-to-thee-my-god-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-glory-to-thee-my-god", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "Glory to Thee, my God, this night, for all the blessings of the light;", "char_len": 70, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/glory_to_thee_my_god_this_night", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-glory-to-thee-my-god-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-glory-to-thee-my-god", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "Forgive me, Lord, for Thy dear Son, the ill that I this day have done;", "char_len": 70, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/glory_to_thee_my_god_this_night", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-glory-to-thee-my-god-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-glory-to-thee-my-god", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "Teach me to live, that I may dread the grave as little as my bed;", "char_len": 65, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/glory_to_thee_my_god_this_night", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-from-every-stormy-wind-s01", "hymn_id": "pd-from-every-stormy-wind", "stanza_index": 1, "en": "From every stormy wind that blows, from every swelling tide of woes,", "char_len": 68, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/from_every_stormy_wind_that_blows", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-from-every-stormy-wind-s02", "hymn_id": "pd-from-every-stormy-wind", "stanza_index": 2, "en": "There is a place where Jesus sheds the oil of gladness on our heads,", "char_len": 68, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/from_every_stormy_wind_that_blows", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-from-every-stormy-wind-s03", "hymn_id": "pd-from-every-stormy-wind", "stanza_index": 3, "en": "There is a scene where spirits blend, where friend holds fellowship with friend,", "char_len": 80, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/from_every_stormy_wind_that_blows", "license": "public_domain"}
{"stanza_id": "pd-from-every-stormy-wind-s04", "hymn_id": "pd-from-every-stormy-wind", "stanza_index": 4, "en": "Ah! whither could we flee for aid, when tempted, desolate, dismayed,", "char_len": 68, "source_url": "https://hymnary.org/text/from_every_stormy_wind_that_blows", "license": "public_domain"}
